    "long_instructions": "# Use Paragraph Tags\r\n\r\nThe `<p>` `</p>` tags or \"paragraph\" start and end tags are placed around text to indicate that it is part of a paragraph. Placing text between paragraph start and end tags lets the computer know that it should be treated differently, often just spacing it out from other text.\r\n\r\n# Do This\r\n\r\n1) Click in between the `<body>` and `</body>` tags - this is where you'll add your code\r\n* Create two paragraphs that ask a question and answer it. This can be a trivia question, a riddle, or a joke.\r\n\t- For example: \"What continent has the largest land mass?\" - \"Asia\"\r\n- Place the text you just wrote inside two separate paragraphs by surrounding each line with `<p>` and `</p>` tags",
